.TH WB\-COMPARE 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-compare \- say what changed between two revisions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR compare [\-\-from <path>] <revision> <revision>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Say what changed between two revisions, each named by its version or its hash: one line for each file added, removed or changed, then a unified diff of each changed file. The installed revision is one; the other is that of the repository at \-\-from, the root of a repository pinned to it. Its files under .watchbill/revision/ are read, and a link is never followed.
.PP
When the revisions are the same, nothing is printed. Otherwise there is one line for each file, sorted by path: added:, removed: or changed: and the path. Then, when a file changed, an empty line and the unified diff of each changed file, headed with a/ and b/ and the path, a being the first revision. The diff is made by git diff \-\-no\-index with fixed options and no configuration, so that it is the same for everyone.
.PP
Ends with 0 when they are the same, 1 when they differ or the files of a revision are refused, 2 when a revision is not found or it was used wrongly. Writes nothing. It asks nothing of the network.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-from <path>
The root of a repository pinned to the other revision. Its version is the line watchbill: of .watchbill/watchbill.yml, and its files must give the hash of the line revision:.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The two revisions are the same.
.TP
.B 1
They differ, or the files of a revision are refused: a refusal is written on standard error as wb compare: limit: and the reason.
.TP
.B 2
A revision is not found (a name that is not held or names two revisions, or a repository that is not set up), or the command was used wrongly.
.SH SEE ALSO
